From: Joseph Lee <joseph.lee@xanadu.ai>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 14:04:35 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] docs: Backline job needs a Slurm account

---
 docs/backline.md | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/docs/backline.md b/docs/backline.md
index 87a0b22..b457669 100644
--- a/docs/backline.md
+++ b/docs/backline.md
@@ -27,9 +27,11 @@ The job script is `qri-backline/examples/job.sh`, cloned to
 `/workspace/qfw-container-base/qri-backline` by `tools/install-backline-venv.sh`:
 
 ```bash
-sbatch /workspace/qfw-container-base/qri-backline/examples/job.sh
+sbatch -A <account> /workspace/qfw-container-base/qri-backline/examples/job.sh
 ```
 
+qfw-slurm requires a Slurm account (`-A`); the provisioned test users use `qfw-test`.
+
 The job makes two requests:
 
 1. **Quantum resources.** The `#SBATCH --qpu=backline-local ...` lines. qfw-slurm reserves
